  contentsAnswer: Clothes for a shoot tomorrow. I packed while my taxi was honking.
  weightAnswer: Six kilos? Honestly, I just grabbed whatever was by the door.
  metalAnswer: Oh. The tripod and camera are still in there. That explains why it
    felt heavier.
  packingAnswer: The tripod is strapped down. The clamps are closed.
  responseAnswer: It should stay still. A tripod does not do much with its legs folded.
  authorReasoning: 'Innocent omission: 10.4 kg contradicts an uncertain guess, but
    the camera/tripod admission explains moderate metal and a quiet pulse.'
